            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0448" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1531/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-29T13:00:00-06:00">September 29, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Reference Department’s circular telegram No. 58, September 28, 6 p.m.<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d408-f1"/> Foreign Office informed the Legation that proposed
                    trade agreement would require ratification by Legislature, which meets on
                    January 1st, 1935, and is in session usually 4 months.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[See also extract from instruction No. 120, December 21, 1934, to the
                        Minister in Costa Rica, printed on <ref target="#pg92">page 92</ref>.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
